Economy'' replaces empirical fits with mandatory structural constants, including the Projection 
Constant ($B \approx 0.2387$) and the Achromatic Phase Snap ($\Phi \approx 14.1^\circ$). We 
provide a rigorous derivation of mass as topological tension, recovering the CODATA values for 
the Dirac CP phase ($270.0^\circ$), the Helium-3 magnetic moment ($\approx -2.127\,\mu_N$), 
and the mass of Technetium-98 ($Q=294$) with metrological precision ($<0.01\%$). The 
framework resolves the ultraviolet (UV) finiteness requirement through a transient $Q=1$ 
neutrino filament (the Jarlskog Shadow), establishing a relativistic-quantum isomorphism via 
Laplace-Beltrami vibrational modes.
