\item \textbf{Lattice Tension ($\lambda_s$):} Enforces the $S^3$ embedding
    \item \textbf{Interaction Stiffness ($k$):} $k \propto \alpha / \ell_f^2$
\end{itemize}
The total SAT Lagrangian becomes:
\begin{multline}
L_{\text{total}} = \frac{\kappa}{2} \left| \mathbf{H}''(\lambda) \right|^2 + \frac{\lambda_s}{2} 
\Big( |X|^2 - R^2(\lambda) \Big)^2 \\
+ \frac{k}{2} \left| \mathbf{H}(\lambda) - \mathbf{G}(\lambda) \right|^2
\end{multline}.
\section{Emergent Invariants and the Zero-Parameter Economy}
\subsection{The Axiomatic Purge of Free Parameters}
To eliminate reliance on empirical curve-fitting, the SAT framework enforces an axiomatic 
removal of free parameters. All constants are recast as geometric invariants derived from the 
filament lattice and $S^3$ manifold packing constraints.
\subsection{Derivation of the Projection Constant ($B$)}
The Projection Constant is defined as:
\begin{equation}
B = \frac{3}{4\pi} \approx 0.23873241
\end{equation}
This value represents the minimal angular separation permitted by the lattice geometry and 
sets the critical velocity scale $v_{\text{crit}} = B \cdot c$.
\subsection{The Obscuration Constant ($\Omega$) and UV Finiteness}
Topological overlap between worldlines is quantified by:
\begin{equation}
\Omega_{ij} = \frac{\int \delta(X_i - X_j, \epsilon) \, d\lambda}{\int d\lambda}
\end{equation}


## Page 5

The regulator $\epsilon \approx 2 \times 10^{-21}\,\mathrm{m}$ enforces UV finiteness by 
preventing singular overlap.
\section{Mass Topology and Standard Model Recovery}
\subsection{Numeric Derivation: The Mass Suppression Function}
Mass is derived in two stages:
\textit{Linear baseline:}
\begin{equation}
m_{\text{linear}} = \frac{Q \cdot m_0}{2B}
\end{equation}
\textit{Braid-smoothing correction:}
\begin{equation}
M_{\text{eff}} = m_{\text{linear}} \cdot S
\end{equation}
with $S \approx 0.2621$.
\textit{Example (Technetium-98):}
\begin{align}
Q &= 294 \\
m_{\text{linear}} &\approx 6.2024 \times 10^{-25}\,\mathrm{kg} \\
M_{\text{eff}} &\approx 1.6256 \times 10^{-25}\,\mathrm{kg}
\end{align}.
\section{Experimental Predictions and Methodology}
\subsection{Signal Isolation: Extraction of the Projection Constant ($B$)}
High-energy scattering in dense molecular lattices allows isolation of $B$ via the 4D topological 
surplus:
\begin{equation}
B = \frac{\sigma_{\text{exp}} - \sigma_{\text{KN}}}{\ell_f^2}
\end{equation}


